      "role": "user",
      "content": "I am currently reviewing a commercial lease agreement for a retail tenant in Singapore. Could you please explain the standard implications of a \"force majeure\" clause in the context of a sudden, prolonged period of business interruption? Specifically, I need to understand how this clause typically affects the tenant's obligation to pay rent during such an event.",
